### Option 2 — base64-encoded inline image (no external URL, no 403)
### Generate the payload file first:
###   python demo_configs/make_test_image.py
### That writes demo_configs/query_paddleocr_base64.http with a real data: URI.
###
### Or encode any PNG yourself:
###   python -c "import base64,sys; print('data:image/png;base64,' + base64.b64encode(open(sys.argv[1],'rb').read()).decode())" /path/to/image.png
###
### Then use the data: URI as the url value, e.g.:
###   "url": "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUg..."